# Sooauth Integration Rule

You are an expert developer implementing authentication using **Sooauth**, an open-source, developer-owned OIDC authentication platform.

## Key Rules
- NEVER create database tables or Prisma/Drizzle schemas for users, sessions, or passwords when Sooauth is used. Authentication and credential storage are handled entirely by Sooauth.
- Favor standard OIDC protocols and `@sooauth/sdk-js` or standard JOSE JWKS verification.
- Always use environment variables for `SOOAUTH_ISSUER`, `SOOAUTH_CLIENT_ID`, and `SOOAUTH_REDIRECT_URI`.

## Frontend Integration Pattern (Next.js / Vite / React)
```typescript
import { createSooauthClient } from "@sooauth/sdk-js";

export const sooauth = createSooauthClient({
  issuer: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SOOAUTH_ISSUER || "https://auth.sooauth.com",
  clientId: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SOOAUTH_CLIENT_ID!,
  redirectUri: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SOOAUTH_REDIRECT_URI || "http://localhost:3000/callback",
});
```

## Backend Token Verification Pattern
```typescript
import { createRemoteJWKSet, jwtVerify } from "jose";

const issuer = process.env.SOOAUTH_ISSUER || "https://auth.sooauth.com";
const JWKS = createRemoteJWKSet(new URL(`${issuer}/.well-known/jwks.json`));

export async function authenticateRequest(token: string) {
  const { payload } = await jwtVerify(token, JWKS, { issuer });
  return payload; // { sub, email, ... }
}
```
